crates/span/src/ast_id.rs, `impl<N> FileAstId<N>` (next to `downcast_unchecked`, ~L369): add a public checked form of its debug assertion, for decoders of persisted ids (hir-def's item tree decode; the known hole in v2/requests/safety.md '## From format-hir-tree': an unchecked ast-id kind decodes, then trips the debug assertion in `ItemTree::index`, a panic in debug and a wrongly typed id in release):

    /// Whether this id's node can be an `M`, as `downcast_unchecked` asserts: what a decoder of
    /// persisted ids checks before calling it.
    #[inline]
    pub fn can_downcast<M: AstIdNode + Into<N>>(self) -> bool {
        self.erase().kind_typed().and_then(|kind| kind.syntax_kind()).is_some_and(|kind| M::can_cast(kind))
    }

(and `downcast_unchecked`'s debug_assert can call it). Tell me by queue when it is in; hir-def's `item_tree/persist.rs::check` then refuses an item whose ast id is not of its kind, as a FormatError.
